        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/dec6dc/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2017-01-19T20:36:36.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I feel like I saw this discussed in some topics way back, but I couldn't find the answer. &nbsp;As far as I can tell, \"Restart Game\" serves as a complete re-seed -- all of the cards/draws/random seeds are different. &nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Sometimes, however, you don't want to scrap everything and start over with a whole new set of cards -- instead you get halfway through a game, and think (ex:) \"Oh, wow - what would have happened if I had just played End of Days instead of Holy Nova 3 turns back?\" &nbsp; Is there an option to \"Restart Game\" that will let you restart with the same draw/random seed?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:48:40.926Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
