        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/d/e47c2d/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2017-01-20T09:53:58.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"McBehrer\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mcbehrer/48/1850_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> McBehrer:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I'd like to be able to turn Advanced on and off, or at least change it from side to side, or for some team villains and not others.</p>\n<p>The Ennead, for instance; I think they're perfect with the front side on advanced, but the back side not.</p>\n<p>Similarly, I'd like to be able to have Proletariat keep multiplying, for instance, and keep Friction's DR 1, but not have Ermine constantly destroying cards.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Do not think you can turn on and off the back side of Advanced Villans such as the Ennead. However if you double click to see the big card on a particular villan during the set up of Team Villans game. You have the option to turn that particular villans Advanced Rule on or off. This does not appear to change all of the villans options.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Which means you could set up a Team Villans game with Advanced Proletariat and Friction but normal Ermine.</p>",
